H4500.definition:
from H5214 (נִיר);
a yoke (properly, for plowing), i.e. the frame of aloom
KJV: beam.

H4501.definition:
or מְנֹרָה; feminine of H4500 (מָנוֹר) (in the original sense of H5216 (נִיר));
a chandelier
KJV: candlestick.

H4502.definition:
from H5144 (נָזַר);
a prince
KJV: crowned.

H4503.definition:
from an unused root meaning to apportion, i.e. bestow;
a donation; euphemistically, tribute; specifically a sacrificial offering (usually bloodless and voluntary)
KJV: gift, oblation, (meat) offering, present, sacrifice.

H4504.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4503 (מִנְחָה);
a sacrificial offering
KJV: oblation, meat offering.

H4505.definition:
from H5162 (נָחַם); comforter;
Menachem, an Israelite
KJV: Menahem.

H4506.definition:
from H5117 (נוּחַ); rest;
Manachath, the name of an Edomite and of a place in Moab
KJV: Manahath.

H4507.definition:
from H4487 (מָנָה);
the Apportioner, i.e. Fate (as an idol)
KJV: number.

H4508.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Minni, an Armenian province
KJV: Minni.

H4509.definition:
from H4480 (מִן) and H3225 (יָמִין); from (the) right hand;
Minjamin, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Miniamin. Compare H4326 (מִיָּמִן).

H4511.definition:
from the same as H4482 (מֵן); enumeration;
Minnith, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Minnith.

H4512.definition:
from H5239 (נָלָה);
completion, i.e. (in produce) wealth
KJV: perfection.

H4513.definition:
a primitive root;
to debar (negatively or positively) from benefit or injury
KJV: deny, keep (back), refrain, restrain, withhold.

H4514.definition:
or מַנְעֻל; from H5274 (נָעַל);
a bolt
KJV: lock.

H4515.definition:
from H5274 (נָעַל);
a bolt
KJV: shoe.

H4516.definition:
from H5276 (נָעֵם);
a delicacy
KJV: dainty.

H4517.definition:
from H5128 (נוּעַ);
a sistrum (so called from its rattling sound)
KJV: cornet.

H4518.definition:
from H5352 (נָקָה);
a sacrificial basin (for holding blood)
KJV: bowl.

H4519.definition:
from H5382 (נָשָׁה); causing to forget;
Menashsheh, a grandson of Jacob, also the tribe descended from him, and its territory
KJV: Manasseh.

H4520.definition:
from H4519 (מְנַשֶּׁה);
a Menashshite or descendant of Menashsheh
KJV: of Manasseh, Manassites.

H4521.definition:
from H4487 (מָנָה);
an allotment (by courtesy, law or providence)
KJV: portion.

H4522.definition:
or מִס; from H4549 (מָסַס);
properly, a burden (as causing to faint), i.e. a tax in the form of forced labor
KJV: discomfited, levy, task(-master), tribute(-tary).

H4523.definition:
from H4549 (מָסַס);
fainting, i.e. (figuratively) disconsolate
KJV: is afflicted.

H4524.definition:
plural masculine מְסִבִּים; or feminine מְסִבּוֹת; from H5437 (סָבַב);
a divan (as enclosing the room); abstractly (adverbial) around
KJV: that compass about, (place) round about, at table.

H4525.definition:
from H5462 (סָגַר);
a fastener, i.e. (of a person) a smith, (of a thing) a prison
KJV: prison, smith.

H4526.definition:
from H5462 (סָגַר);
something enclosing, i.e. a margin (of a region, of a panel); concretely, a stronghold
KJV: border, close place, hole.

H4527.definition:
from H3245 (יָסַד);
a foundation
KJV: foundation.

H4528.definition:
from the same as H5468 (סֶדֶר);
a colonnade or internal portico (from its rows of pillars)
KJV: porch.

H4529.definition:
a primitive root;
to dissolve
KJV: make to consume away, (make to) melt, water.

H4530.definition:
from H4549 (מָסַס) (in the sense of flowing);
abundance, i.e. (adverbially) liberally
KJV: tribute.

H4531.definition:
from H5254 (נָסָה);
a testing, of men (judicial) or of God (querulous)
KJV: temptation, trial.

H4532.definition:
the same as H4531 (מַסָּה);
Massah, a place in the Desert
KJV: Massah.

H4533.definition:
apparently from an unused root meaning to cover;
a veil
KJV: vail.

H4534.definition:
for H4881 (מְשׂוּכָה);
a hedge
KJV: thorn hedge.

H4535.definition:
from H5255 (נָסַח) in the sense of staving off;
a cordon, (adverbially) or (as a) military barrier
KJV: broken down.

H4537.definition:
a primitive root;
to mix, especially wine (with spices)
KJV: mingle.

H4538.definition:
from H4537 (מָסַךְ);
a mixture, i.e. of wine with spices
KJV: mixture.

H4539.definition:
from H5526 (סָכַךְ);
a cover, i.e. veil
KJV: covering, curtain, hanging.

H4540.definition:
from H5526 (סָכַךְ);
a covering, i.e. garniture
KJV: covering.

H4541.definition:
from H5258 (נָסַךְ);
properly, a pouring over, i.e. fusion of metal (especially a cast image); by implication, a libation, i.e. league; concretely a coverlet (as if poured out)
KJV: covering, molten (image), vail.

H4543.definition:
by transp. from H3664 (כָּנַס);
a magazine
KJV: store(-house), treasure.

H4545.definition:
from H5259 (נָסַךְ) in the sense of spreading out;
something expanded, i.e. the warp in aloom (as stretched out to receive the woof)
KJV: web.

H4546.definition:
from H5549 (סָלַל);
a thoroughfare (as turnpiked), literally or figuratively; specifically a viaduct, a staircase
KJV: causeway, course, highway, path, terrace.

H4547.definition:
from H5549 (סָלַל);
a thoroughfare (as turnpiked)
KJV: highway.

H4548.definition:
or מִסְמֵר; also (feminine) מַסְמְרָה; or מִסְמְרָה; or even מַשְׂמְרָה; (Ecclesiastes 12:11), from H5568 (סָמַר);
a peg (as bristling from the surface)
KJV: nail.

H4549.definition:
a primitive root;
to liquefy; figuratively, to waste (with disease), to faint (with fatigue, fear or grief)
KJV: discourage, faint, be loosed, melt (away), refuse, [idiom] utterly.

H4550.definition:
from H5265 (נָסַע);
a departure (from striking the tents), i.e. march (not necessarily a single day's travel); by implication, a station (or point of departure)
KJV: journey(-ing).

H4551.definition:
from H5265 (נָסַע) in the sense of projecting;
a missile (spear or arrow); also a quarry (whence stones are, as it were, ejected)
KJV: before it was brought, dart.

H4552.definition:
' from H5582 (סָעַד);
a balustrade (for stairs)
KJV: pillar.

H4553.definition:
from H5594 (סָפַד);
a lamentation
KJV: lamentation, one mourneth, mourning, wailing.

H4554.definition:
from an unused root meaning to collect;
fodder
KJV: provender.

H4555.definition:
from H5596 (סָפַח);
a veil (as spread out)
KJV: kerchief.

H4556.definition:
from H5596 (סָפַח);
scruf (as spreading over the surface)
KJV: scab.

H4557.definition:
from H5608 (סָפַר);
a number, definite (arithmetical) or indefinite (large, innumerable; small, a few); also (abstractly) narration
KJV: [phrase] abundance, account, [idiom] all, [idiom] few, (in-) finite, (certain) number(-ed), tale, telling, [phrase] time.

H4558.definition:
the same as H4457 (מֶלְקָח); number;
Mispar, an Israelite
KJV: Mizpar. Compare H4559 (מִסְפֶּרֶת).

H4559.definition:
feminine of H4437 (מַלְכוּ); enumeration;
Mispereth, an Israelite
KJV: Mispereth. Compare H4458 (מֶלְתָּחָה).

H4560.definition:
a primitive root;
to sunder, i.e. (transitively) set apart, or (reflex.) apostatize
KJV: commit, deliver.

H4562.definition:
from H631 (אָסַר);
a band
KJV: bond.

H4563.definition:
from H5641 (סָתַר);
a refuge
KJV: covert.

H4564.definition:
from H5641 (סָתַר);
properly, a hider, i.e. (abstractly) a hiding, i.e. aversion
KJV: hid.

H4565.definition:
from H5641 (סָתַר);
properly, a concealer, i.e. a covert
KJV: secret(-ly, place).

H4566.definition:
from H5647 (עָבַד);
an act
KJV: work.

H4567.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4566 (מַעְבָּד);
an act
KJV: work.

H4568.definition:
from H5666 (עָבָה);
properly, compact (part of soil), i.e. loam
KJV: clay.

H4569.definition:
or feminine מַעֲבָרָה; from H5674 (עָבַר);
a crossing-place (of a river, a ford; of a mountain, a pass); abstractly, a transit, i.e. (figuratively) overwhelming
KJV: ford, place where...pass, passage.

H4570.definition:
or feminine מַעְגָּלָה; from the same as H5696 (עָגֹל);
a track (literally or figuratively); also a rampart (as circular)
KJV: going, path, trench, way(-side).

H4571.definition:
a primitive root;
to waver
KJV: make to shake, slide, slip.

H4572.definition:
from H5710 (עָדָה); ornamental;
Maadai, an Israelite
KJV: Maadai.

H4573.definition:
from H5710 (עָדָה) and H3050 (יָהּ); ornament of Jah;
Maadjah, an Israelite
KJV: Maadiah. Compare H4153 (מוֹעַדְיָה).

H4574.definition:
or (feminine) מַעֲדַנָּה; from H5727 (עָדַן);
a delicacy or (abstractly) pleasure (adverbially, cheerfully)
KJV: dainty, delicately, delight.

H4575.definition:
by transitive from H6029 (עָנַד);
a bond, i.e. group
KJV: influence.

H4576.definition:
from H5737 (עֲדַר);
a (weeding) hoe
KJV: mattock.

H4577.definition:
(Aramaic) or מְעָא; (Aramaic), corresponding to H4578 (מֵעֶה)xlit mêʻâh corrected to mêʻeh;
only in plural the bowels
KJV: belly.

H4578.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to be soft;
used only in plural the intestines, or (collectively) the abdomen, figuratively, sympathy; by implication, a vest; by extension the stomach, the uterus (or of men, the seat of generation), the heart (figuratively)
KJV: belly, bowels, [idiom] heart, womb.

H4579.definition:
feminine of H4578 (מֵעֶה)xlit mêʻâh corrected to mêʻeh;
the belly, i.e. (figuratively) interior
KJV: gravel.

H4581.definition:
(also מָעוּז ); or מָעֹז (also מָעֻז; from H5810 (עָזַז);
a fortified place; figuratively, a defence
KJV: force, fort(-ress), rock, strength(-en), ([idiom] most) strong (hold).

H4582.definition:
from H4600 (מָעַךְ); oppressed;
Maok, a Philistine
KJV: Maoch.

H4583.definition:
or מָעִין; (1 Chronicles 4:41), from the same as H5772 (עוֹנָה);
an abode, of God (the Tabernacle or the Temple), men (their home) or animals (their lair); hence, a retreat (asylum)
KJV: den, dwelling((-) place), habitation.

H4584.definition:
the same as H4583 (מָעוֹן); a residence;
Maon, the name of an Israelite and of a place in Palestine
KJV: Maon, Maonites. Compare H1010 (בֵּית בַּעַל מְעוֹן), H4586 (מְעוּנִי)lemma מְעוּנָי third vowel, corrected to מְעוּנִי.

H4585.definition:
or מְעֹנָה; feminine of H4583 (מָעוֹן), and meaning the same
{an abode, of God (the Tabernacle or the Temple), men (their home) or animals (their lair); hence, a retreat (asylum)}
KJV: den, habitation, (dwelling) place, refuge.

H4586.definition:
or מְעִינִי; probably patrial from H4584 (מָעוֹן);
a Meunite, or inhabitant of Maon (only in plural)
KJV: Mehunim(-s), Meunim.

H4587.definition:
plural of H4585 (מְעוֹנָה); habitative;
Meonothai, an Israelite
KJV: Meonothai.

H4588.definition:
from H5774 (עוּף) in the sense of covering with shade (compare H4155 (מוּעָף));
darkness
KJV: dimness.

H4589.definition:
from H5783 (עוּר);
nakedness, i.e. (in plural) the pudenda
KJV: nakedness.

H4590.definition:
or מַעַזְיָהוּ; probably from H5756 (עוּז) (in the sense of protection) and H3050 (יָהּ); rescue of Jah;
Maazjah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Maaziah.

H4591.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to pare off, i.e. lessen; intransitively, to be (or causatively, to make) small or few (or figuratively, ineffective)
KJV: suffer to decrease, diminish, (be, [idiom] borrow a, give, make) few (in number, -ness), gather least (little), be (seem) little, ([idiom] give the) less, be minished, bring to nothing.

H4592.definition:
or מְעָט; from H4591 (מָעַט);
a little or few (often adverbial or compar.)
KJV: almost (some, very) few(-er, -est), lightly, little (while), (very) small (matter, thing), some, soon, [idiom] very.

H4593.definition:
passive adjective of H4591 (מָעַט);
thinned (as to the edge), i.e. sharp
KJV: wrapped up.

H4594.definition:
from H5844 (עָטָה);
a vestment
KJV: garment.

H4595.definition:
from H5848 (עָטַף);
a cloak
KJV: mantle.

H4596.definition:
from H5753 (עָוָה); (compare H5856 (עִי))
a pile of rubbish (as contorted), i.e. a ruin
KJV: heap.

H4597.definition:
probably from H4578 (מֵעֶה)xlit mêʻâh corrected to mêʻeh; sympathetic;
Maai, an Israelite
KJV: Maai.

H4598.definition:
from H4603 (מָעַל) in the sense of covering;
a robe (i.e. upper and outer garment)
KJV: cloke, coat, mantle, robe.

H4599.definition:
or מַעְיְנוֹ; (Psalm 114:8), or (feminine) מַעְיָנָה; from H5869 (עַיִן) (as a denominative in the sense of a spring);
a fountain (also collectively), figuratively, a source (of satisfaction)
KJV: fountain, spring, well.
